--- [factual] In exactly two sentences: why is LLM decode memory-bandwidth-bound while prefill is compute-bound?
> LLM decoding is memory-bandwidth-bound because it involves fetching and processing large sequences of tokens, which is limited by the speed at which data can be moved between memory and the processing units. Conversely, prefill is compute-bound because it involves the initial processing and context building, which is primarily limited by the computational power required for matrix multiplications and attention mechanisms.
